  "notes": "The hook-writer, and the research hands this entry its headline parameter outright: \"a melodic, slide-heavy 808 that mirrors the vocal hook's contour — a good template for '808 follows topline' generation\". So `slideProb` is 0.7 with `followsLeadRoot` set, second only to `2-chainz` in this batch, and the slide intervals are the stepwise `M2`/`m3` a topline moves by rather than the octave a sub drops. The three parameters that separate this from `migos` are the ones the research separates them on: hats \"triplet-based but slightly less dense than the group records\" (`fillDensity` 0.58 against Migos's 0.72); \"minor pentatonic hooks\" leading the scale weights where the group entry leads with aeolian/harmonic minor; and \"4-bar loops … with long sustained tails\" against the group's 2-bar cells, which is `phraseBars` weighted to 4 with `articulation: legato`. \"Heavy autotune quantization to the scale\" is `chordToneBias` 0.82 with `halfStepDissonance` at 0.03 — the line does not sit between notes. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium`: the research rates this high-medium, documenting the role rather than the sessions. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the rim accent as a perc density, the family weights, the whole `intervals`/`contour` split, and the entire kick block — the research says only \"standard 3-backbeat trap kit\" here, so the `3&` secondary anchor and the 0.42 syncopation are authored to keep this beat distinguishable from its two group-mates rather than because a source names them. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
